on of the distributions is 100% qualified dividends.\n\nPart II Box 15\n\nBased on information available at the time of this posting, a portion of the distributions made during 2021 are expected to be a non-dividend distribution. A non-dividend distribution will first be applied against the shareholder’s basis under Section 301(c)(2).\n\n<table id=\"e1\">\n<tr><th>Declared Date</th><th>Payment Date</th><th>Cash Distrib per share</th><th>Non-dividend %</th></tr>\n<tr><td>4/21/2021</td><td>5/18/2021</td><td>$ 0.619</td><td>100%</td></tr>\n<tr><td>5/13/2021</td><td>7/16/2021</td><td>$ 0.08</td><td>100%</td></tr>\n<tr><td>9/23/2021</td><td>10/18/2021</td><td>$ 0.08</td><td>100%</td></tr>\n</table>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMAC Stock: Dividend Yield, History & Performance | Dividend Vision (https://www.dividendvision.com/assets/tickers?ticker=MAC)\nciteturn136search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Image: MAC logo ... Last Ex-Dividend [Button: ?] ... 2023  | $0.68  | $0.68  | +9.7%  |\n\nActual distributions are grouped by ex-date. Regular growth excludes specials and capital gains; YTD compares through the same calendar date last year. Partial launch years remain visible but cannot produce a growth percentage. [Button: ?]\n\nAnnual distributions per share by ex-date\nPeriod  | Regular  | Total cash  | Regular growth[Button: ?]  | Comparability\n--- | --- | --- | --- | ---\n2026 YTD  | $0.51  | $0.51  | 0.0%  | vs prior-year YTD\n2025  | $0.68  | $0.68  | 0.0%  | \n2024  | $0.68  | $0.68  | 0.0%  | \n2023  | $0.68  | $0.68  | +9.7%  | \n2022  | $0.62  | $0.62  | +3.3%  | \n2021  | $0.6  | $0.6  | -47.8%  | \n2020  | $1.15  | $1.15  | -61.7%  | \n2019  | $3  | $3  | +1.0%  | \n2018  | $2.97  | $2.97  | +3.5%  | \n2017  | $2.87  | $2.87  | +4.4%  | \n2016  | $2.75  | $2.75  | -62.4%  | \n2015  | $7.31  | $7.31  | +191.2%  | \n2014  | $2.51  | $2.51  | +6.4%  | \n2013  | $2.36  | $2.36  | +5.8%  | \n2012  | $2.23